ARCHITECTURE NOTICE ("BLACK PEARL IN A GLASS CASE"):
This distribution separates the 100% auditable, open benchmark harness and thin C-ABI
wrapper ("Glass Case", executable under `--network=none`) from the precompiled, stripped,
section-header-obliterated (`e_shoff=0`) machine-code compute core ("Black Pearl").

1. GRANT OF SINGLE-NODE EVALUATION LICENSE
   Subject to strict compliance with all eight (8) protection shields below, The Authors
   ("Licensor") hereby grant you a personal, non-exclusive, non-transferable,
   non-sublicensable, revocable, royalty-free license to execute the unmodified
   evaluation binaries solely for individual non-commercial benchmark verification
   and peer performance reproduction.

2. SHIELD 1 — STRICT ANTI-REVERSE ENGINEERING, DECOMPILATION & DISASSEMBLY
   You shall NOT decompile, disassemble, decrypt, reconstruct ELF section header tables
   (SHT), attach hardware or software debuggers/tracers, extract lookup-table (LUT)
   constants, or reverse-engineer any portion of the precompiled binaries or machine code.
   To the maximum extent permitted by applicable contract law (cf. Bowers v. Baystate
   Technologies, Inc., 320 F.3d 1317), you expressly waive any statutory fair-use or
   interoperability defense to reverse-engineering.

3. SHIELD 2 — NO IMPLIED PATENT LICENSE, ZERO EXHAUSTION & ANTI-ESTOPPEL
   All algorithmic architectures, SIMD/SIMT register schedules, sub-byte lookup tables,
   and numerical kernels are proprietary trade secrets and patent-pending inventions.
   No license, immunity, or exhaustion of rights under any patent or patent application
   is granted or implied by estoppel, exhaustion, or otherwise. Any re-implementation
   of the underlying methods infringes Licensor's pending and issued patent claims.

4. SHIELD 3 — GOVERNING LAW, ARBITRATION & EXCLUSION OF CISG
   This License shall be governed by and construed in accordance with applicable
   international intellectual property conventions and the laws of the Licensor's
   principal sovereign jurisdiction, excluding conflict-of-law rules and expressly
   excluding the United Nations Convention on Contracts for the International Sale of
   Goods (CISG).

5. SHIELD 4 — SEVERABILITY & SURVIVAL OF PROTECTIONS
   If any provision of this License is held invalid or unenforceable, such provision
   shall be reformed to the maximum enforceable extent to effectuate Licensor's
   protection intent, and all remaining shields shall remain in full force and survive
   any termination of this License.

6. SHIELD 5 — TECHNOLOGICAL PROTECTION MEASURES (17 U.S.C. SECTION 1201 & COPYRIGHT ACT S. 41.1)
   The ELF64 Section Header Table obliteration (`e_shoff=0`), Cold-Path Mixed Boolean-
   Arithmetic (MBA) initialization guards, anti-tracer sentinels (`PR_SET_DUMPABLE=0`),
   and Ed25519 cryptographic gates constitute effective Technological Protection Measures
   ("TPM") under 17 U.S.C. Section 1201 (DMCA) and Section 41.1 of the Copyright Act.
   Any bypass, patching, symbol reconstruction, or circumvention of these TPMs is a
   direct statutory violation independent of contract breach.

7. SHIELD 6 — ANTI-AI CLEAN-ROOM, AUTOMATED SYNTHESIS & BINARY TRANSLATION BAN
   You shall NOT feed, expose, or provide the binaries, their C-ABI signatures,
   disassembly listings, control-flow graphs, PMU hardware counter traces, or timing
   profiles into any Large Language Model (LLM), AI coding agent, neural decompiler,
   SMT/CEGIS superoptimizer, or binary translation layer (including ZLUDA-style
   transpilers) to synthesize clean-room functional specifications, train models, or
   transpile kernels to another instruction set architecture (ISA).

8. SHIELD 7 — SINGLE-NODE CAP (1 SOCKET / 1 GPU / QUEUE-DEPTH=1), ANTI-PROXY & DARK COMPUTE BAN
   Evaluation is strictly bounded to one (1) physical CPU socket and one (1) physical
   GPU accelerator with `Queue-Depth=1` in an isolated interactive session. You shall NOT:
   a. Wrap the binary behind any network socket, reverse proxy (NGINX, Envoy, gRPC, HTTP),
      IPC queue, or shared-memory multiplexer to serve multiple workers or users;
   b. Deploy or execute the binary in any internal corporate, institutional, or government
      "Dark Compute" environment (including internal R&D clusters, CI/CD pipelines, batch
      preprocessing, or cloud cost-reduction workloads) without a paid Commercial Enterprise
      License from Licensor.

9. SHIELD 8 — ENTERPRISE SCA TRAPDOOR (LicenseRef-Silicium-Community-1.0) & VIRAL BENCHMARKING
   a. Automated Compliance Trapdoor: All headers carry `SPDX-License-Identifier:
      LicenseRef-Silicium-Community-1.0` to trigger mandatory Software Composition Analysis
      (SCA) policy blocks in enterprise CI/CD scanners (Black Duck, FOSSA, Snyk) unless a
      Commercial Enterprise License certificate is registered.
   b. Asymmetric Viral Benchmarking: Public publication of performance benchmarks of the
      unmodified binary on social platforms, technical forums, and academic papers is
      expressly permitted and encouraged provided `reproduce_all.sh` is cited. Using the
      binary to calibrate, autotune, or validate a competing engine is strictly prohibited.

